[size=6][b]Compass — HUD Compass for StarRupture[/b][/size]

[b]Found a bug? Report it on GitHub: [url=https://github.com/AlienXAXS/StarRupture-Plugin-Compass/issues]https://github.com/AlienXAXS/StarRupture-Plugin-Compass/issues[/url][/b] and attach your [b]ModLoader.log[/b] (in [b]Binaries\Win64\ModLoader\Logs\[/b]).

Adds a heads-up compass bar to your HUD showing nearby players, enemies, and points of interest based on the direction you're facing.

[b]Client-side only[/b] — no server install required.

[quote][b]If you encounter issues or just have a question, please discuss this in our Discord which you can find on the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starrupture/mods/89]Modloaders Description Page[/url] here on Nexus.[/b][/quote]
[line]

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Players — other players in your session[/*]
[*]Base Cores — player base cores[/*]
[*]Map Markers — antennas, abandoned bases, caves, obelisks[/*]
[*]Foundables — dead bodies and drones[/*]
[*]Enemies — hostile entities[/*]
[*]Custom Pins — your own placed map pins[/*]
[/list]
Each category can be toggled and given its own render distance.

[line]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download the latest file from the [b]Files[/b] tab[/*]
[*]Open the ZIP file[/*]
[*]Copy the contents of the included Plugins folder into:
[i]"StarRupture\Binaries\Win64\ModLoader\Plugins"[/i][/*]
[*]Launch the game once to generate the config file[/*]
[*]Open:
[i]"Plugins\config\Compass.ini"[/i][/*]
[*]Set:
[i]"Enabled=1"[/i][/*]
[/list]
[line]

[size=5][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

The config file is created automatically on first launch:

[i]"Plugins\config\Compass.ini"[/i]

You can customise:

[list]
[*]Enabled — turn the compass on/off (0 or 1)[/*]
[*]Position / Width / Scale — adjust size and placement[/*]
[*]Line Colour — HEX colour of the compass bar[/*]
[*]Render Distance — per-category limit (0 = unlimited)[/*]
[/list]
[line]

[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Compass not visible[/b] — make sure [i]"Enabled=1"[/i] is set[/*]
[*][b]Plugin not loading[/b] — check [i]"modloader.log in Binaries\Win64\"[/i][/*]
[/list]
[line]

